DTSTAMP:19700101T000000Z
DTSTART:20261019T115900Z
DTEND:20261019T125900Z
SUMMARY:WWW 2027 · Full-paper abstract deadline
DESCRIPTION:ACM Web Conference (formerly International World Wide Web Confe
 rence)\nMeeting: 2027-05-10 to 2027-05-14\, Dublin\, Ireland\nStatus: con
 firmed\, checked 2026-10-30\nFormat: Paper-based\nOfficial source: https:
 //www2027.thewebconf.org/research-track-papers/\nVenue Radar: https://gon
 -uri.github.io/venue-radar/#www-2027\nNotes: Full-paper abstract and pape
 r deadlines (Oct 18/25 AoE) have passed with no extension. The short-pape
 r OpenReview portal was observed open on 2026-10-30\; separate mandatory 
 abstract gates apply. Resource papers (four pages\, non-anonymous\, compa
 nion proceedings) are due Dec 17 AoE\; their portal is not public yet. Op
 enReview's short-paper forms close about an hour after the AoE cutoffs st
 ored here. Demo papers (Nov 16 per the website)\, the PhD symposium (Jan 
 6 per the website) and the general workshop-paper date (Jan 4\, workshops
  not yet listed) are not tracked as separate routes\; the OpenReview demo
  and PhD symposium forms are set to close Nov 15\, 21:00 UTC. The Web4Goo
 d track is discontinued. Research must substantively address the Web\, no
 t merely use a web dataset. Preserve WWW as the stable series alias. Size
  is an editorial estimate.
CATEGORIES:Information Retrieval & Search,Recommender Systems,Graphs & Grap
 h Learning,LLM Agents & Tool Use
URL:https://www2027.thewebconf.org/research-track-papers/
END:VEVENT
